coverage.other_conditions:
Excluded from the definition:
(a) aggregated, anonymous rental data reports that make no recommendations;
(b) products used to set rent or income limits under government affordable-housing guidelines;
(c) information used for market research for project financing, appraisals, or research, testing or training for software development, provided Competitor Data is not an input when a recommendation is calculated.

rules.exemptions:
Excluded from the definition:
- aggregated and anonymous rental data reports that do not recommend rents, fees, occupancy rates or other terms;
- products used to set rent or income limits under affordable-housing guidelines;
- products or processes used for market research for project financing, appraisals, or software research, testing or training, where Competitor Data is not an input when a recommendation is calculated.

rules.requirement:
Rental housing providers in Berkeley may not ask about or use criminal history or criminal background checks in advertising, applications, tenant selection or decision-making.

As to current or prospective tenants, it is unlawful to:
- inquire about criminal history;
- indicate that people with criminal backgrounds will not be considered;
- refuse to rent, or terminate a tenancy, based on criminal history;
- require disclosure of, or authorization to release, criminal history;
- demand a higher deposit or rent based on criminal history;
- refuse to add an immediate family member because of that person's criminal history;
- disqualify tenants from rental assistance programs such as Section 8 based on criminal history, subject to exceptions;
- otherwise treat applicants or tenants differently based on criminal history.

A landlord taking any action based on criminal history must give the applicant or tenant written notice and an opportunity to respond.

Providers must prominently post the Notice to Rental Applicants and Tenants on:
- application materials;
- websites;
- locations they control that applicants frequently visit.

The Rent Board administers complaints.

rules.exemptions:
Exempt situations:
- lifetime sex offenders;
- limited exemptions for public housing and Section 8 properties;
- owner-occupied properties of 1-3 units where an owner of record resides in one unit as primary residence;
- units under a rental agreement allowing owners to move back per BMC 13.76.130 A.9;
- units occupied by existing tenants seeking to sublet or add or replace roommates.

coverage.summary:
Rent control (rent ceilings and AGA) applies only to fully covered units:
- most units in multifamily properties built before 1980;
- single-family homes whose current tenancy began before 1996;
- rooming houses (single-family homes with five or more rooms rented individually under separate leases).

Partially covered units are registered but have no rent control:
- new construction with a certificate of occupancy after June 1980 (per D009);
- single-family tenancies beginning on or after Jan 1, 1996;
- most condominiums;
- certain subsidized units.

Exempt unit types are outside the ordinance.

rules.exemptions:
Partially covered (no rent control):
- new construction with a certificate of occupancy after June 1980 (D006 says after 1980);
- single-family tenancies beginning on or after Jan. 1, 1996;
- most condominiums;
- Section 202 and 811 units;
- Rent Supplement, Section 8 Loan Management Set Aside and Project-based Section 8 units in HUD-mortgage projects.

Exempt:
- Golden Duplex;
- owner shares kitchen or bath and lived on the property at the start of the tenancy;
- ADU-property tenancies after Nov. 7, 2018 with an owner-occupied unit;
- university rental units;
- nonprofit cooperatives.

coverage.summary:
Covers both fully and partially covered units, including:
- pre-1980 multifamily units;
- single-family homes regardless of tenancy start date;
- rooming houses;
- post-June 1980 new construction;
- most condominiums;
- government-subsidized units.
Only exempt unit types are excluded. No construction cutoff applies.

rules.exemptions:
Exempt:
- Golden Duplex;
- owner shares kitchen or bath and lived on the property at the start of the tenancy;
- tenancies after Nov. 7, 2018 on properties with an ADU and an owner-occupied unit;
- university rental units;
- nonprofit cooperatives.

Exempt:
- Golden Duplex;
- owner shares kitchen or bath and lived on the property at the start of the tenancy;
- ADU-property tenancies after Nov. 7, 2018 with an owner-occupied unit;
- university rental units;
- nonprofit cooperatives.
